---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---
<Base
  title={`About ${SITE.name}`}
  description="Learn how Howloop builds transparent Australian financial calculators, verifies public CDR bank rates, and maintains independent editorial standards."
>
  <div class="hl-wrap hl-prose-wrap">
    <article class="hl-prose">
      <h1>About Howloop</h1>
      <p>
        <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> (<a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.domain}</a>) is an independent Australian financial education and calculator platform designed to help households model everyday money decisions in plain English.
      </p>

      <div class="hl-policy-callout">
        <strong>General Information Notice:</strong> Howloop provides mathematical modelling tools, public data summaries, and educational guides. We do not hold an Australian Financial Services Licence (AFSL) and do not provide personal financial, taxation, or credit advice. Always verify product Product Disclosure Statements (PDS) and Target Market Determinations (TMD) directly with the issuing institution.
      </div>

      <h2>What We Build &amp; Maintain</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Client-Side Financial Calculators:</strong> Six transparent calculators covering Australian resident take-home pay (FY 2025–26 &amp; FY 2026–27 Stage 3 tax brackets, Medicare levy, HELP/HECS repayments, and Superannuation Guarantee), mortgage offset vs savings comparisons, compound interest, emergency fund sizing, and home deposit LVR.</li>
        <li><strong>13-Week Cash-Flow &amp; Payday Planner:</strong> A practical calendar workspace that maps fortnightly or monthly pay cycles against quarterly Australian household bills (electricity, council/strata rates, water, and vehicle registration).</li>
        <li><strong>Public CDR Banking Explorer:</strong> Dated snapshots retrieved from the Australian Government Consumer Data Right (CDR) register, clearly distinguishing unambiguous base variable rates from conditional bonus tiers.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Editorial &amp; Data Integrity Principles</h2>
      <p>
        Every calculator on Howloop documents its exact mathematical assumptions, statutory tax/super thresholds, and rounding behaviour on our <a href="/methodology/">Calculation Methodology</a> page. When an external CDR bank endpoint is unreachable or older than seven days, our interface explicitly flags the snapshot age rather than claiming live whole-market coverage.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in Touch</h2>
      <p>
        Spotted a calculation edge case, an updated bank product rule, or a guide you would like us to write? Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> or visit our <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
